 "response": "**Getosti's budget is now $2095K.**\n\n**Which records count**\n- Only Finance Office budget entries change the budget. Messages from Facilities, PMO, Sales, Engineering, Legal, Marketing, Operations and Vendor calls do not.\n- Some Finance Office entries are not budget changes, such as room moves, cost-center codes, audits and receipts. They are ignored too.\n\n**How withdrawal chains were resolved**\nEach chain is worked from its latest withdrawal backwards. A withdrawal that is not itself withdrawn removes its target. Some chains that matter:\n- #0161 \u2192 #0081 \u2192 #0032 \u2192 #0015 \u2192 #0009 \u2192 #0007 \u2192 #0002: the +$472K in #0002 stays.\n- #1164 \u2192 #0154 \u2192 #0021 \u2192 #0013 \u2192 #0012 \u2192 #0003: #0003 (+$547K) is withdrawn.\n- #0776 \u2192 #0037 \u2192 #0019 \u2192 #0006: #0006 (+$27K) is withdrawn.\n- #1250 \u2192 #0150 \u2192 #0087 \u2192 #0080 \u2192 #0071: #0071 (+$436K) stays.\n- #1438 \u2192 #0784 \u2192 #0708 \u2192 #0534 \u2192 #0165 \u2192 #0033: #0033 (\u2212$259K) is withdrawn.\n- #0938 \u2192 #0848 \u2192 #0756 \u2192 #0528 \u2192 #0431: #0431 (\u2212$51K) stays.\n- #1500 \u2192 #1102 \u2192 #0624 \u2192 #0339: #0339 (+$69K) is withdrawn.\n- #1491 \u2192 #1477 \u2192 #0812 \u2192 #0568: #0568 (+$18K) is withdrawn.\n\nAll other chains were handled the same way. In total, 108 budget updates end up withdrawn.\n\n**Calculation**\nI started from the $1730K set in #0001. I then applied every remaining increase and decrease once, in record order. The running total ends at $2095K after the last effective update, #1590 (\u2212$25K).\n\nANSWER: $2095K",
